{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"SB0073","billNumberShort":"S.B. 73","billNumberLong":"SB0073S03","fileNumber":"2026FL0643","shortTitle":"Online Age Verification Amendments","currentSubVersion":"3","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"MUSSECR","primeSponsorName":"Sen. Musselman, Calvin R.","primeSponsorHouse":"S","floorSponsor":"ELIASS","floorSponsorName":"Rep. Eliason, Steve","floorSponsorHouse":"H","generalProvisions":"This bill enacts provisions related to online providers of content harmful to minors.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>defines terms;<hr><ltbullet>provides legislative findings;<hr><ltbullet>imposes an excise tax on certain entities that provide content harmful to minors; <hr><ltbullet>provides for administration and collection of the excise tax by the State Tax Commission based on referrals from the Division of Consumer Protection; <hr><ltbullet>creates the Minor Mental Health Restricted Account within the General Fund; <hr><ltbullet>directs tax revenues to the Department of Health and Human Services and the Division of Consumer Protection to be used for mental health programs and enforcement of age verification requirements; <hr><ltbullet>provides for liability for publishers and distributors of material harmful to minors who fail to perform age verification; <hr><ltbullet>grants the Division of Consumer Protection authority to investigate and enforce age verification requirements; <hr><ltbullet>provides administrative fines and civil penalties for violations of age verification requirements; <hr><ltbullet>creates the Minor Online Safety Restricted Account (account) within the General Fund and provides for deposits from tax revenue and from fines and civil penalties; <hr><ltbullet>directs money in the account to the Division of Consumer Protection to be used for enforcement of age verification requirements and online safety for minors;<hr><ltbullet>provides rulemaking authority to the Division of Consumer Protection to establish standards for substantial portion determinations and age verification methods;<hr><ltbullet>provides safe harbor for approved age verification methods; <hr><ltbullet>provides a severability clause; and <hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"","draftingAttorney":"Scott Elder","fiscalAnalyst":"Alejandra G Rodriguez","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/19/2026","trackingID":"MOUADPLSCW","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-05 11:44:26.610","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-05 11:44:26.610","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LLFA","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"LFA/ bill assigned to staff for fiscal analysis for SB0073","owner":"Legislative Fiscal Analyst","actionDate":"2026-01-05 11:44:27.677","actionClass":"F","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LFA1","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"LFA/ bill sent to agencies for fiscal input for SB0073","owner":"Legislative Fiscal Agency","actionDate":"2026-01-05 11:44:27.677","actionClass":"F","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LFA2","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Senate/ received bill from Legislative Research","owner":"Waiting for Introduction in the Senate","actionDate":"2026-01-07 10:09:34.000","actionClass":"S","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"SRECLRGC","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"LFA/ fiscal note sent to sponsor for SB0073","owner":"Version Sponsor","actionDate":"2026-01-19 12:09:3